---
term: Opponent
aka:
  - Adversary
section: building-blocks
order: 44
definition: A party that opposes a charter in a conflict that some amendment the charter allows could reconcile through arbitration.
seeAlso:
  - status
  - enemy
  - limit-of-arbitration
---
A charter and its opponents settle their conflict through noncooperative struggle until an arbitrated reconciliation moves the opponent to [[neutral]] or [[associate]] status. The conflict lies within the [[limit of arbitration]].
